---
// Fall week 1: teams are announced and sit together for the first time.
// Five minutes of information, fifteen to find the team on the seating map,
// twenty for Two truths and a bug, then the Team Charter kickoff for the rest
// of the session. Served at /decks/fall-week-1/. The seating map is the live
// decks/auditorium-seating.html, served by src/pages/decks/.
import FrameSlide from "../components/deck/FrameSlide.astro";
import Notes from "../components/deck/Notes.astro";
import QrSlide from "../components/deck/QrSlide.astro";
import Slide from "../components/deck/Slide.astro";
import StatementSlide from "../components/deck/StatementSlide.astro";
import TermSessions from "../components/deck/TermSessions.astro";
import TitleSlide from "../components/deck/TitleSlide.astro";
import TwoColumnSlide from "../components/deck/TwoColumnSlide.astro";

export const title = "Team Introductions and Charter";

const charter = new URL("/assignments/team-charter/", Astro.site).href;
---

<TitleSlide
  kicker="CS 461, fall week 1"
  title="Team Introductions and Charter"
  subtitle="Meet your team, then start the agreement you'll work under"
  byline="Kirsten Winters and Alex Ulbrich, your instructors"
>
  <Notes time="0:15">
    <p>Five minutes of information, then the room moves.</p>
  </Notes>
</TitleSlide>

<Slide kicker="Today" title="Agenda">
  <ol>
    <li>Information from the instruction team</li>
    <li>Find your team and sit together</li>
    <li>Icebreaker: Two truths and a bug</li>
    <li>Start the Team Charter, and ask questions</li>
  </ol>
  <Notes time="0:30" cue="Information is five minutes; keep to it.">
    <p>
      The budget: 5 minutes of information, 15 to find your team, 20 for the
      icebreaker (the activity itself is fifteen minutes; the other five are
      for settling and wants), then the charter for the rest of the session.
    </p>
  </Notes>
</Slide>

<Slide kicker="This week" title="Email your project partner">
  <ul>
    <li>Meet as a team, then draft from the introduction email template</li>
    <li class="fragment">Send it by the end of week 1, every teammate on Cc</li>
    <li class="fragment">Be professional, be brief, and adapt the template as you see fit</li>
    <li class="fragment">
      Does every teammate already meet with them? Don't send it: message the
      instructors at cs-46x-help@oregonstate.edu by the end of week 1
    </li>
  </ul>
  <Notes time="1:15" cue="Send it today if you can.">
    <p>
      The template is linked from Term Startup and already carries the
      questions worth asking before the first meeting. The meeting you're
      asking for has to fit someone else's calendar, so send it as soon as you
      know your team. Your partner's contact details arrive by email.
    </p>
  </Notes>
</Slide>

<Slide kicker="Due next" title="Weeks 1 and 2" wide>
  <TermSessions term="fall" from={1} to={2} rows={["Due", "In class"]} />
  <Notes time="1:30">
    <p>
      From the schedule. Week 2 is the first TA check-in, which goes through
      the Term Startup list while it's still in progress.
    </p>
  </Notes>
</Slide>

<TwoColumnSlide kicker="This term" title="Check announcements" divider>
  <div slot="left">
    <h3>This week</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Your team's TA, who sets up your check-ins</li>
      <li>Your project partner's contact details</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div slot="right">
    <h3>Several teams, one project?</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Agree with your partner what your team owns</li>
      <li>Agree how the teams talk to each other</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <Notes time="1:15">
    <p>
      Which projects may split into two teams this year is in announcements.
      A team on a multi-team project negotiates what it owns (an interface, a
      repository, or a milestone) and writes its part into its Definition of
      Shipped in winter.
    </p>
  </Notes>
</TwoColumnSlide>

<StatementSlide kicker="Teams are announced">
  Find your team number on the map, and sit together.
  <Notes time="0:15">
    <p>Next slide is the live map. Leave it up while people move.</p>
  </Notes>
</StatementSlide>

<FrameSlide
  src="/decks/auditorium-seating.html?slide"
  label="Auditorium seating map by team number"
>
  <Notes time="15:00" cue="Hover a team's seats to highlight them for a lost team.">
    <p>
      The live seating map. Hovering a block highlights one team; left and
      right are as the room faces the screen. Fifteen minutes to find seats
      and say hello.
    </p>
  </Notes>
</FrameSlide>

<Slide kicker="Icebreaker, fifteen minutes" title="Two truths and a bug">
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Write three claims each:</strong> two true and one invented, all about your life with computers</li>
    <li class="fragment"><strong>Guess before the reveal:</strong> the team votes on the lie, then the author says. A minute each, no deliberating</li>
    <li class="fragment"><strong>Chase the interesting one:</strong> ask for the story behind the claim that caused the most argument</li>
    <li class="fragment"><strong>End with a want:</strong> one sentence each on what you most want to be better at by the end of the project</li>
  </ul>
  <Notes time="20:00" cue="Call time at fifteen, then give five for wants.">
    <p>
      Specific beats impressive: "I took down production with a missing
      semicolon", "I learned to program on a graphing calculator", "I have
      never once used a debugger". Nobody collects the wants; people say them
      out loud so teammates know what each person is here for.
    </p>
  </Notes>
</Slide>

<Slide kicker="Team Charter kickoff" title="Three artifacts, one submission">
  <ol>
    <li><strong>The charter:</strong> roles, decision process, cadence and tools, conflict and accountability, inclusion norms, AI and confidentiality</li>
    <li class="fragment"><strong><code>CONTRIBUTING.md</code>:</strong> setup, the PR workflow, the Definition of Done, and the Contribution Norm</li>
    <li class="fragment"><strong>The AI context file:</strong> <code>AGENTS.md</code> or your tool's equivalent</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="deck-small after-list fragment">
    You won't know everything yet. Write down what you know, and name what
    gets added later and who adds it.
  </p>
  <Notes time="3:00" cue="Teams start writing after the next slide.">
    <p>
      The charter is 2 to 4 pages; the other two live in the repository. In
      week 2 there may be little code: a Definition of Done can name the gate
      the team will add, the sprint it lands in, and its owner. Set Up Your
      Repository's Skills prepares the AI context file and is this week's
      optional activity.
    </p>
  </Notes>
</Slide>

<Slide kicker="Team Charter kickoff" title="Three roles, one owner each">
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Project Manager:</strong> the board and the partner communication cadence</li>
    <li class="fragment"><strong>AI Coordinator:</strong> the AI context file and the confidentiality boundary</li>
    <li class="fragment"><strong>Quality Owner:</strong> CI health, the Definition of Done, and releases</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="deck-small after-list fragment">
    Rotate at least once a term. Everyone chairs at least one decision per
    term.
  </p>
  <Notes time="2:00">
    <p>
      Keep these three names: the defense asks about them. On a team of five,
      the students who hold none of the three name an ownership area instead,
      so everyone owns something nameable.
    </p>
  </Notes>
</Slide>

<QrSlide kicker="Start now" title="The Team Charter page" url={charter}>
  <p>Every required section, and the rubric it's scored on.</p>
  <Notes time="1:00" cue="Teams work on the charter for the rest of the session.">
    <p>Walk the room; the instruction team takes questions table by table.</p>
  </Notes>
</QrSlide>

<Slide kicker="Sources" title="Where this deck comes from">
  <ul class="deck-small">
    <li>The introduction email: Term Startup</li>
    <li>Due weeks and class sessions: Schedule</li>
    <li>Several teams on one project: For Students</li>
    <li>The icebreaker: Two truths and a bug, in Team and Workflow activities</li>
    <li>The charter, its sections and roles: Team Charter</li>
    <li>The seating map: decks/auditorium-seating.html</li>
  </ul>
  <Notes time="0:15">
    <p>Leave the charter QR code up instead if teams are still scanning.</p>
  </Notes>
</Slide>

<style>
  /* A closing line under a list, set apart from its last item. */
  .after-list {
    margin-block-start: 56px;
  }
</style>
